```
Where `Scale` is a custom class with the following definition:
```cpp
class Scale {
public:
    enum Type { Category, Numeric };
    Type GetType() const;
    int min;
    int max;
};
```
You need to implement the `filterJSON` function to filter the `dataArray` based on the `xScale` range and return the filtered JSON objects as a vector.

### Solution:
```cpp
std::vector<nlohmann::json> filterJSON(const std::vector<nlohmann::json>& dataArray, const Scale& xScale) {
    std::vector<nlohmann::json> filteredData;
    for (size_t i = 0; i < dataArray.size(); ++i) {
        const nlohmann::json& groupData = dataArray[i];
        std::size_t start = 0, end = groupData.size() - 1;
        if (xScale.GetType() == Scale::Type::Category) {
            start = std::max(start, static_cast<std::size_t>(xScale.min));
            end = std::min(end, static_cast<std::size_t>(xScale.max));
        }
        nlohmann::json filteredGroupData;
        for (std::size_t j = start; j <= end; ++j) {
            filteredGroupData.push_back(groupData[j]);
        }
        filteredData.push_back(filteredGroupData);
    }
    return filteredData;
}
```
In the solution, the `filterJSON` function iterates through the `dataArray` and filters the JSON objects based on the `xScale` range. If the `xScale` type is a category, it adjusts the start and end indices based on the scale range and then constructs the filtered JSON objects. Finally, it returns the filtered JSON objects as a vector.

