Write a method `processExcelData()` that reads the Excel file specified by `excelFilePath` and `excelWorksheet`, extracts data from the columns specified by `excelColumnName` and `excelColumnBemerkung`, and performs the following operation:
- If the value in the `excelColumnName` column is "Completed", then print the value from the `excelColumnBemerkung` column.
- If the value in the `excelColumnName` column is not "Completed", then print "Task pending".

Assume that the Excel file contains headers in the first row and the data starts from the second row.

### Solution:
```java
import org.apache.poi.ss.usermodel.*;

import java.io.File;
import java.io.FileInputStream;
import java.io.IOException;

public class ExcelProcessor {
    @Value("${excel.filepath}")
    private String excelFilePath;

    @Value("${excel.worksheet}")
    private String excelWorksheet;

    @Value("${excel.worksheet.column.name}")
    private int excelColumnName;

    @Value("${excel.worksheet.column.bemerkung}")
    private int excelColumnBemerkung;

    public void processExcelData() {
        try (FileInputStream file = new FileInputStream(new File(excelFilePath))) {
            Workbook workbook = WorkbookFactory.create(file);
            Sheet sheet = workbook.getSheet(excelWorksheet);

            for (int i = 1; i <= sheet.getLastRowNum(); i++) {
                Row row = sheet.getRow(i);
                Cell nameCell = row.getCell(excelColumnName);
                Cell bemerkungCell = row.getCell(excelColumnBemerkung);

                if (nameCell != null && nameCell.getCellType() == CellType.STRING) {
                    String nameValue = nameCell.getStringCellValue();
                    if (nameValue.equals("Completed")) {
                        if (bemerkungCell != null && bemerkungCell.getCellType() == CellType.STRING) {
                            String bemerkungValue = bemerkungCell.getStringCellValue();
                            System.out.println(bemerkungValue);
                        }
                    } else {
                        System.out.println("Task pending");
                    }
                }
            }
        } catch (IOException | EncryptedDocumentException | InvalidFormatException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```

In the solution, the `processExcelData()` method reads the Excel file specified by `excelFilePath` and `excelWorksheet`. It then iterates through the rows, extracts data from the specified columns, and performs the required operations based on the extracted information. The Apache POI library is used to handle Excel file operations. If the value in the `excelColumnName` column is "Completed", it prints the value from the `excelColumnBemerkung` column; otherwise, it prints "Task pending".

