You are tasked with implementing a depth-first search algorithm to visit all the children of a given construct. The construct is represented as a tree structure, where each node has a unique identifier and may have zero or more children. Your goal is to write a function that takes the construct and a starting node identifier as input and returns the order in which the nodes are visited during the depth-first search.

The construct is represented using the following data structure:
```java
