2. Deposit funds into an account by specifying the account number and the amount to deposit.
3. Withdraw funds from an account by specifying the account number and the amount to withdraw.
4. Check the balance of an account by specifying the account number.

Your program should also handle error cases such as attempting to withdraw more funds than are available in the account and attempting to access a non-existent account.

