Your task is to implement the `RecipeItem` and `Shape` structures and their associated methods to support the recipe management system. The `RecipeItem` structure represents an item used in recipes, and the `Shape` structure represents the shape of ingredients on the crafting grid.

Define the `RecipeItem` structure with the following fields:
- `name: String` - The name of the item
- `quantity: u32` - The quantity of the item required in the recipe

Define the `Shape` structure with the following fields:
- `rows: u32` - The number of rows in the shape
- `columns: u32` - The number of columns in the shape
- `grid: Vec<Vec<Option<RecipeItem>>>` - A 2D grid representing the arrangement of ingredients on the crafting grid. Each cell may contain an optional `RecipeItem` or be empty.

Implement the following methods for the `RecipeItem` structure:
- `new(name: String, quantity: u32) -> RecipeItem` - A constructor to create a new `RecipeItem` instance
- `display(&self) -> String` - A method to display the name and quantity of the item

Implement the following methods for the `Shape` structure:
- `new(rows: u32, columns: u32, grid: Vec<Vec<Option<RecipeItem>>>) -> Shape` - A constructor to create a new `Shape` instance
- `display(&self) -> String` - A method to display the shape of ingredients on the crafting grid

### Solution:
```rust
use serde::{Serialize, Deserialize};

#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct RecipeItem {
    name: String,
    quantity: u32,
}

impl RecipeItem {
    fn new(name: String, quantity: u32) -> RecipeItem {
        RecipeItem { name, quantity }
    }

    fn display(&self) -> String {
        format!("{} x{}", self.name, self.quantity)
    }
}

#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct Shape {
    rows: u32,
    columns: u32,
    grid: Vec<Vec<Option<RecipeItem>>>,
}

impl Shape {
    fn new(rows: u32, columns: u32, grid: Vec<Vec<Option<RecipeItem>>>) -> Shape {
        Shape { rows, columns, grid }
    }

    fn display(&self) -> String {
        let mut display_str = String::new();
        for row in &self.grid {
            for cell in row {
                match cell {
                    Some(item) => display_str.push_str(&item.display()),
                    None => display_str.push_str("Empty"),
                }
                display_str.push('\t');
            }
            display_str.push('\n');
        }
        display_str
    }
}

fn main() {
    let item1 = RecipeItem::new("Flour".to_string(), 2);
    let item2 = RecipeItem::new("Egg".to_string(), 1);

    let shaped_recipe = ShapedRecipe {
        result: item1,
        in_shape: Shape::new(3, 3, vec![
            vec![Some(item1.clone()), Some(item1.clone()), Some(item1.clone())],
            vec![Some(item1.clone()), Some(item2.clone()), Some(item1.clone())],
            vec![Some(item1.clone()), Some(item1.clone()), Some(item1.clone())],
        ]),
        out_shape: Some(Shape::new(2, 2, vec![
            vec![Some(item1.clone()), Some(item1.clone())],
            vec![Some(item1.clone()), Some(item1.clone())],
        ])),
    };

