You are tasked with creating a program that simulates a simple queue data structure using a linked list. The queue should support the standard operations of enqueue (add an element to the end of the queue) and dequeue (remove an element from the front of the queue). Additionally, the program should implement a method to print the elements of the queue.

You are provided with the following Node class definition to represent the elements of the linked list:

```java
class Node {
    int data;
    Node next;

    public Node(int data) {
        this.data = data;
        this.next = null;
    }
}
```

You need to implement the Queue class with the following methods:
1. `enqueue(int data)`: Add an element with the given data to the end of the queue.
2. `dequeue()`: Remove and return the element from the front of the queue. If the queue is empty, return -1.
3. `printQueue()`: Print all the elements of the queue in the order they were added.

You should implement the Queue class to achieve the desired functionality.

### Solution:
```java
class Queue {
    private Node front;
    private Node rear;

    public Queue() {
        this.front = null;
        this.rear = null;
    }

    public void enqueue(int data) {
        Node newNode = new Node(data);
        if (rear == null) {
            front = newNode;
            rear = newNode;
        } else {
            rear.next = newNode;
            rear = newNode;
        }
    }

    public int dequeue() {
        if (front == null) {
            return -1; // Queue is empty
        }
        int data = front.data;
        front = front.next;
        if (front == null) {
            rear = null; // Queue is now empty
        }
        return data;
    }

    public void printQueue() {
        Node current = front;
        while (current != null) {
            System.out.print(current.data + " ");
            current = current.next;
        }
        System.out.println();
    }
}
```
This implementation of the Queue class uses a linked list to simulate the queue data structure. The `enqueue` method adds elements to the end of the queue, the `dequeue` method removes elements from the front of the queue, and the `printQueue` method prints all the elements of the queue.

