You are working on a software system that involves processing modules. Each processing module is represented by an entity class called `ProcessingModule`, which contains various attributes and methods for handling the processing tasks. Your task is to implement a method that calculates the average processing time for a list of processing modules.

The `ProcessingModule` class has the following attributes and methods:
- `name`: a string representing the name of the processing module
- `processingTime`: an integer representing the time taken for processing in milliseconds
- `getProcessingTime()`: a method that returns the processing time for the module

You need to create a method `calculateAverageProcessingTime` that takes a list of `ProcessingModule` objects as input and returns the average processing time for all the modules in the list.

Your task is to implement the `calculateAverageProcessingTime` method and ensure that it correctly calculates the average processing time for the given list of processing modules.

### Solution:
```java
import java.util.List;

public class ProcessingModule {
    private String name;
    private int processingTime;

    public ProcessingModule(String name, int processingTime) {
        this.name = name;
        this.processingTime = processingTime;
    }

    public int getProcessingTime() {
        return processingTime;
    }

    public static double calculateAverageProcessingTime(List<ProcessingModule> modules) {
        if (modules == null || modules.isEmpty()) {
            return 0; // Return 0 for an empty list or null input
        }

        int totalProcessingTime = 0;
        for (ProcessingModule module : modules) {
            totalProcessingTime += module.getProcessingTime();
        }

        return (double) totalProcessingTime / modules.size();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Example usage
        ProcessingModule module1 = new ProcessingModule("Module1", 100);
        ProcessingModule module2 = new ProcessingModule("Module2", 200);
        ProcessingModule module3 = new ProcessingModule("Module3", 150);

        List<ProcessingModule> moduleList = List.of(module1, module2, module3);
        double averageProcessingTime = calculateAverageProcessingTime(moduleList);
        System.out.println("Average Processing Time: " + averageProcessingTime);
    }
}
```

