You are tasked with implementing a Java class called `MaskReader` that reads a text file and masks specific sensitive information. The class should provide a method `maskSensitiveInfo` that takes in the file path of the input text file and the file path of the output text file. The method should read the input file, mask any sensitive information, and write the masked content to the output file.

Sensitive information to be masked includes any occurrences of credit card numbers and email addresses. Credit card numbers are defined as any sequence of 16 digits in the format "XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX" where X represents a digit. Email addresses are defined as any sequence of characters followed by the "@" symbol and then a domain name.

The `MaskReader` class should have the following method:
```java
