    public void maskSensitiveInfo(String inputFilePath, String outputFilePath) {
        // Your implementation here
    }
}
```

Your task is to complete the `maskSensitiveInfo` method to read the input file, mask any credit card numbers and email addresses, and write the masked content to the output file. The masked credit card numbers should be replaced with "XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX" and the masked email addresses should be replaced with "*****@*****".

Assume that the input file contains text data in a readable format and may contain multiple occurrences of credit card numbers and email addresses.

### Solution:
```java
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.BufferedWriter;
import java.io.FileReader;
import java.io.FileWriter;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.regex.Matcher;
import java.util.regex.Pattern;

public class MaskReader {
    public void maskSensitiveInfo(String inputFilePath, String outputFilePath) {
        try (BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(inputFilePath));
             BufferedWriter writer = new BufferedWriter(new FileWriter(outputFilePath))) {
            String line;
            while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                line = maskCreditCardNumbers(line);
                line = maskEmailAddresses(line);
                writer.write(line);
                writer.newLine();
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }

    private String maskCreditCardNumbers(String line) {
        Pattern pattern = Pattern.compile("\\b\\d{4}-\\d{4}-\\d{4}-\\d{4}\\b");
        Matcher matcher = pattern.matcher(line);
        return matcher.replaceAll("XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX");
    }

    private String maskEmailAddresses(String line) {
        Pattern pattern = Pattern.compile("\\b[\\w.-]+@[\\w.-]+\\.[a-zA-Z]{2,6}\\b");
        Matcher matcher = pattern.matcher(line);
        return matcher.replaceAll("*****@*****");
    }
}
```

In the solution, the `maskSensitiveInfo` method reads each line from the input file, applies the `maskCreditCardNumbers` and `maskEmailAddresses` methods to mask the sensitive information, and writes the masked content to the output file. The `maskCreditCardNumbers` and `maskEmailAddresses` methods use regular expressions to find and replace the sensitive information with the masked values.

